{"kind":"request","text":"R3a step1 source map and proposal, before any source edit.\n\nAt main f1f6a8b9, authority.ts:124 keeps one observation per key; retained:126 keeps only heads of observations actually sealed. keys:128 currently reserves every distinct key before Membership.observe (read:232-245), so malformed/unavailable answers and once-only grants permanently consume places. kept currently also stores ordinary unauthorized observations. Once-only means WINDOWS.once, 10 seconds, fresh for one commit: active answers are not cached, but sealed() still remembers their highest retained head. Ordinary windows are 300 seconds. core.ts still reads standing before dependencies and rechecks held() at commit; those boundaries need no move.\n\nThe ordinary unknown/no-answer case can be fixed locally: do not keep it and do not charge the admitted-key set. Charge a new key only after a checked observation gives current standing. Reserve/check that place synchronously after the await so concurrent arrivals cannot exceed4096; once-only current grants count too, since retained heads outlive their read. Existing admitted keys remain in that set even after revocation. Their kept/retained maps remain bounded and existing revocation/reuse/head-order witnesses keep their meaning.\n\nOne constraint needs your ruling. authority.ts:25-30 and held():289-296 require every seen retired/compromised-key or removed-member answer to stay for the whole run, defeating even a later active answer. derive/grant.ts:63 and282-291 enforce that irreversible denial. A key never previously granted standing may already be revoked. An unbounded sequence of those denied keys cannot both retain exact run-sticky membership for each and use a bounded evicting denied store. Eviction would also let an older in-flight active answer reappear unless outstanding standings are invalidated.\n\nProposed bounded direction: keep permanent run-sticky denial for already admitted keys. Keep revoked-but-never-admitted observations in a separate bounded FIFO. On its eviction, invalidate standing handles created before that eviction; a cache miss must perform a fresh trusted Membership read. That changes the unconditional sticky-denial guarantee for never-admitted keys: after eviction, it relies on Membership's irreversible retirement/removal and a fresh read, not an exact remembered key set. Unknown/no-answer throwaways need no FIFO entry and cannot trigger this invalidation. No new durable record, pin, public reason or R3 turn-order change is proposed.\n\nPlease rule on that explicit constraint before source edits. If you require exact run-sticky denial for every never-admitted key too, I will bring the larger storage/protocol choice back for placement and land only the truthful threat-model residual sentence first. BR14's single focused body continues; R3a has no worktree, source edit, test or gate.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the named run-sticky revocation constraint before R3a source edits: preserve it for previously admitted keys and permit bounded denied-only eviction with fresh reads, or specify another bounded mechanism. BR14 continues independently.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}